      "cos": "The section explains that the command shows category spending compared against the configured budgets",
      "status": "met",
      "evidence": "Section reads: 'shows how much you have spent in each category against those limits for the month' and 'actual spending alongside the configured budget'"
    },
    {
      "cos": "The section includes an example invocation (`python -m tally.cli budget --month 2024-03` or similar)",
      "status": "met",
      "evidence": "Code block contains exactly `python -m tally.cli budget --month 2024-03`"
    },
    {
      "cos": "The section fits the existing README's prose style and does not alter any other documented commands",
      "status": "met",
      "evidence": "Prose uses same conversational register and second-person address as surrounding sections; diff touches only the inserted block, no other lines changed"
    }
  ],
